{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>If there be among you a needy man.</b> The needy of your own city take precedence." "<b>Of one of your brothers.</b> Your paternal brother takes precedence over your maternal brother." "<b>Your gates.</b> The poor of your city take precedence over the poor of another city." "<b>You shall not harden.</b> There is a person who is in anguish whether he gives or does not give — therefore it says ״לֹא תְאַמֵּץ.״ There is one who stretches out his hand and clenches it — therefore it says ״לֹא תִקְפֹּץ״ (ibid.)." "<b>Your brother, the needy man.</b> If you do not give him, you will end up being the brother of the needy man (ibid.)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:10.621440040Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}